WEBVTT

1
00:00:01.400 --> 00:00:03.582
Meet RVTSS — the Revit MCP for Claude.

2
00:00:03.632 --> 00:00:06.296
It connects Claude directly to your live Revit model,

3
00:00:06.346 --> 00:00:09.745
so you can inspect, edit, and check your projects…

4
00:00:09.795 --> 00:00:11.499
just by asking.

5
00:00:11.549 --> 00:00:15.579
In the next few minutes, you'll install it, connect it,

6
00:00:15.629 --> 00:00:17.406
and run your first commands.

7
00:00:17.906 --> 00:00:20.581
Before we start, you need four things.

8
00:00:20.631 --> 00:00:24.085
Autodesk Revit, version 2021 or newer.

9
00:00:24.135 --> 00:00:26.979
pyRevit, version 4.8 or newer.

10
00:00:27.029 --> 00:00:29.829
Python 3.11, with the uv package manager.

11
00:00:29.879 --> 00:00:34.053
And Claude — either Claude Desktop, or Claude Code.

12
00:00:34.553 --> 00:00:35.933
Here's how it works.

13
00:00:35.983 --> 00:00:40.140
Claude talks to the RVTSS MCP server on your computer.

14
00:00:40.190 --> 00:00:42.989
The server sends requests to pyRevit Routes

15
00:00:43.039 --> 00:00:47.856
a small web service running inside Revit, on port 48884.

16
00:00:47.906 --> 00:00:51.906
And Routes runs every command through the Revit API, safely,

17
00:00:51.956 --> 00:00:53.507
inside a transaction.

18
00:00:54.007 --> 00:00:56.750
Step one: install the extension.

19
00:00:56.800 --> 00:01:01.051
Open PowerShell, go to your pyRevit extensions folder,

20
00:01:01.101 --> 00:01:05.003
and clone the repository as RVTSS dot extension.

21
00:01:05.053 --> 00:01:06.988
Keep only ONE copy

22
00:01:07.038 --> 00:01:10.431
if an older Revit MCP extension is installed, remove it first,

23
00:01:10.481 --> 00:01:12.296
or the two will conflict.

24
00:01:12.796 --> 00:01:15.382
Step two: turn on Routes.

25
00:01:15.432 --> 00:01:20.122
In Revit, open the pyRevit tab, then Settings, then Routes.

26
00:01:20.172 --> 00:01:26.268
Enable the Routes Server, set the host to 127.0.0.1, save,

27
00:01:26.318 --> 00:01:27.871
and reload pyRevit.

28
00:01:27.921 --> 00:01:31.019
A new RVTSS tab appears in the ribbon.

29
00:01:31.519 --> 00:01:33.937
Step three: check the server.

30
00:01:33.987 --> 00:01:36.324
Open the status page shown on screen.

31
00:01:36.374 --> 00:01:41.466
You should see health: healthy, and the RVTSS version.

32
00:01:41.516 --> 00:01:43.622
If it says the route does not exist,

33
00:01:43.672 --> 00:01:46.368
enable the extension in pyRevit's extension manager,

34
00:01:46.418 --> 00:01:47.930
and restart Revit.

35
00:01:48.430 --> 00:01:51.251
Step four: run the self-test.

36
00:01:51.301 --> 00:01:54.665
On the RVTSS tab, click Diagnostics, then Run Self-Test.

37
00:01:54.715 --> 00:01:59.065
It works on a copy of the bundled test model

38
00:01:59.115 --> 00:02:01.017
your own files are never touched

39
00:02:01.067 --> 00:02:03.227
and opens a pass or fail report.

40
00:02:03.728 --> 00:02:06.125
Step five: connect Claude.

41
00:02:06.175 --> 00:02:08.950
In the extension folder, run uv sync.

42
00:02:09.000 --> 00:02:14.839
Then, in Claude Desktop, open Settings, Developer, Edit Config,

43
00:02:14.889 --> 00:02:17.200
and add the RVTSS server.

44
00:02:17.250 --> 00:02:18.394
Using Claude Code?

45
00:02:18.444 --> 00:02:19.823
One command does it.

46
00:02:19.873 --> 00:02:23.028
Restart Claude, and the RVTSS tools appear.

47
00:02:23.528 --> 00:02:25.991
RVTSS has 77 tools in 10 toolsets.

48
00:02:26.041 --> 00:02:27.825
Every tool costs context,

49
00:02:27.875 --> 00:02:32.514
so load only what you need with the RVTSS TOOLSETS setting.

50
00:02:32.564 --> 00:02:37.289
Pick a profile: BIM coordinator, family author, modeler,

51
00:02:37.339 --> 00:02:41.045
or minimal… or keep the default, all.

52
00:02:41.545 --> 00:02:43.345
Now, just talk to Claude.

53
00:02:43.395 --> 00:02:45.565
Give me an overview of this project.

54
00:02:45.615 --> 00:02:49.535
Find all doors on Level 2 wider than 900 millimetres.

55
00:02:49.585 --> 00:02:52.489
Check clashes between ducts and structural framing,

56
00:02:52.539 --> 00:02:54.015
and export a report.

57
00:02:54.065 --> 00:02:56.658
Claude picks the right tools, runs them in Revit,

58
00:02:56.708 --> 00:02:57.869
and reports back.

59
00:02:58.370 --> 00:02:59.915
Here's what's inside.

60
00:02:59.965 --> 00:03:03.476
Model intelligence, to find anything in your model.

61
00:03:03.526 --> 00:03:06.195
Element editing, with bulk updates.

62
00:03:06.245 --> 00:03:08.060
Full family creation.

63
00:03:08.110 --> 00:03:12.505
Shared, project, and global parameters.

64
00:03:12.555 --> 00:03:17.156
Documentation automation for views, sheets, and schedules.

65
00:03:17.206 --> 00:03:19.433
And coordination and QC: clash detection,

66
00:03:19.483 --> 00:03:23.516
ISO 19650 naming checks, and Excel and IFC exports.

67
00:03:24.016 --> 00:03:25.812
And it's built to be safe.

68
00:03:25.862 --> 00:03:29.347
Every change runs in a named transaction you can undo.

69
00:03:29.397 --> 00:03:32.966
Dry runs let Revit validate a change, then roll it back.

70
00:03:33.016 --> 00:03:36.230
Large or destructive edits need your confirmation.

71
00:03:36.280 --> 00:03:38.365
Dimensions always need units.

72
00:03:38.415 --> 00:03:40.971
And you can lock it all down with a token.

73
00:03:41.471 --> 00:03:43.267
That's it — you're ready.

74
00:03:43.317 --> 00:03:47.412
The full user manual and every link are on the RVTSS website.

75
00:03:47.462 --> 00:03:49.478
Install it, connect Claude…

76
00:03:49.528 --> 00:03:51.368
and start talking to your models.

